---
title: Fennel sausage and pepperoni pizza
tags: [italian, pork]
cuisine: italian
source: The Stewart by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/the-stewart
---

> A restaurant batch: kilograms of dough and 40 lb of sausage. Scale down
> before you start. The dough needs three days in the fridge.

== Dough ==

Stir the @sourdough starter{1.755%kg} into the @water{17.5%kg} in a large bowl.
Set aside 300 g of this starter liquid.

Put the rest in a #stand mixer{} with the dough hook. Mix on low, add the
@high-gluten flour{23.8%kg} and @00 flour{3.2%kg}, and mix until just combined.

Mix ~{4%minutes} more. Add the @extra virgin olive oil{35%g} and mix
~{7%minutes}.

Add the @kosher salt{690%g} and the reserved starter liquid. Mix on high
~{9%minutes}, until the dough passes the windowpane test.

Cover in an oiled bowl and leave ~{4%hours} at room temperature.

Divide into 380 g pieces on a floured counter, roll into balls, wrap, and
refrigerate ~{3%days}.

== Fennel sausage ==

Season the @ground pork{40%lb} with the @brown sugar{555%g},
@calabrian chili{420%g}(crushed), @fennel seeds{150%g}, @garlic powder{150%g},
@onion powder{150%g} and @kosher salt{100%g}.

> The source lists "fennel pepper"; fennel seed is the likely reading.

Add a splash of @water{}(warm) and mix by hand until even. Cover and
refrigerate ~{24%hours}.

Heat the oven to 450°F. Flatten the meat into even patties on a foil-lined
#sheet tray{} and cook ~{30%minutes}.

Let them cool, then break them up in the stand mixer with the dough hook.
Refrigerate.

== Tomato sauce ==

Heat some @extra virgin olive oil{} in a #sauté pan{} over medium-high heat.
Cook the @red onion{}(chopped) ~{4%minutes}, until soft.

Add the @garlic{}(confit) and @calabrian chili{}, season with
@ground oregano{}, @kosher salt{} and @black pepper{}, and cook ~{3%minutes}.

Add the @San Marzano tomatoes{28%oz}(whole, one can) and bring to a boil.
Lower the heat and simmer ~{1%hour}.

Off the heat, stir in the @basil{}(fresh leaves) and blend smooth with an
#immersion blender{}. Refrigerate.

== Lemon-garlic ricotta ==

Mix the @ricotta{5%lb}, @lemon juice{160%g}, @garlic oil{60%g},
@garlic{30%g}(grated), @lemon zest{25%g} and @kosher salt{18%g}. Spoon into a
#piping bag{} and refrigerate.

== Pizza ==

Heat the pizza oven.

Stretch one dough ball into a 14-inch round on a floured counter. Spread 165 g
of the tomato sauce over it and scatter 80 g of the sausage.

Add the @pepperoni{50%g}(cup-and-char), some @basil{}(fresh leaves),
@garlic oil{4%g}, @ground oregano{1%g} and @parmesan{5%g}(grated).

Bake until done to your liking. Top with three spoonfuls of the ricotta, a
little more @parmesan{}(grated) and @red chile flakes{}.
